From e4c8afd8620666d380bc2c2b837c572ad2916d3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iOSNJBrepo <42407902+iOSNJBrepo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:47:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] uke: Start all eight cores and enable inter-processor
 interrupts

Secondary cores intermittently took a synchronous external abort on
their first fetch at a kernel address (arm_init_tramp). common_start
reads cpu_ttep with the MMU and caches off, and ArmCpu never cleaned it
to memory before PSCI CPU_ON, so a core could load a stale TTBR1 root.
Clean it with the other early-boot data.

With the cores starting reliably, armcpu-self-ipi=1 delivers IPIs on all
eight cores. The new self-IPI mode 2 (secondaries signal the boot core)
stays opt-in; the default remains off.

Add a per-core entry trace (sheng_smp_entry) from the reset vector to
arm_init_cpu, shown in the SHENG-SMP log. A secondary keeps the V=P
vectors until arm_init_tramp has run, so an early fault is recorded and
an instruction-fetch external abort is retried.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
